<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Room at the end of the control bar for the player's own buttons.

      Media3 reserves `exo_small_icon_width` (48dp) past `exo_basic_controls`
      and `exo_extra_controls_scroll_view`, which is exactly one button of ours.
      There are two now — rotate and playback mode — so a second 48dp has to be
      reserved as well, or the leftmost of the two lands on top of Media3's own
      icons.

      Measured rather than derived. With one button the group ends exactly
      where `exo_basic_controls` does. With two, the UI tree showed the rotate
      button at x 2094–2238 sitting under Media3's own button at 2106–2250 — an
      overlap of a whole button, because only one had been reserved for.

      **104dp, not 96dp.** Reserving two lots of `exo_small_icon_width` looks
      right and is not: the buttons are 52dp, and Media3's constant is 48dp, so
      each one under-reserves by 4dp. Measured after changing it to 96dp, the
      overlap was down to 13px — the two 4dp shortfalls, still visible.
    -->
    <dimen name="player_custom_button_room">104dp</dimen>
</resources>
